A||N||4||reddog||Distributor Questions?????||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||12-14-2001||08:04 PM||||Can anyone tell me what the symptoms would be of a failing pickup coil! Also should a distributor be able to wiggle at all (back and forth/side to side) mine seems to move about an inch. and I can never get the hold down bolt tight enough to prevent the distributor from being rotated by hand!! <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||12-14-2001||08:18 PM||||Does the hold down bolt go on top of the hold down bracket? Maybe that bracket was put in upside down. The distributor should not move. What else can you see there?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||reddog||12-14-2001||09:28 PM||||Well all you can see is the bolt and the bracket on top of the shaft. don't think it is on upside down. I think I am just going to replace the whole distributor it's probably time anyway. I am still having a miss in the ignition since I had the MSD 6A installed tried with stock coil and ignition module as well as an accel coil and ign. module.It cuts out with both though its more noticable with the accel stuff. BTW the miss occurs randomly at any speed in any gear and at no specific time . Just randomly. It's like it jerks for a split second and the tach jumps around and the check engine light flashes for a fraction of a second . The engine then just resumes at speed. Tried to pull codes but none is set. It's like the ignition just quits for a millisecond and then it is fine. Didn't do it until the MSD was hooked up!  <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||12-15-2001||05:15 AM||||Make sure the coil to distributor wire is connected and seated properly. Also, the two connections going into the Ignition Module may be loose (check and see if the clips on the connectors are broken). If the Pick-up coil goes out you will know it - the car won't start.......<P>Also, no, the distributor should not be loose but when (if) you had it out did you replace the o-ring? - just checking, that can be a source of a major oil leak. As for being loose, has the distributor plate disengaged from the distributor shaft?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||reddog||12-15-2001||07:11 AM||||yep it broke off or something like that! it was welded back together a while back!Don't know exactely seems like the mechanic said the plate broke loose and instead of replacing it he welded it back so that I wouldn't have to shell out $100.00 for a new one! Come to think of it, it seems some of my timing problems started right around the same time that he rewelded the distributor. However It never seemed to miss until I had the MSD put on. Any ideas why?<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
